29
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:16,000
Classmates, you all said it very well. In fact, our attitude towards facing difficulties is more important than anything.

30
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:20,500
The book mentions the character Liu Zhongyuan, do you like him?

31
00:03:21,500 --> 00:03:32,000
I quite like the characterization of Liu Zhongyuan. Because from initially being uninterested in poetry, after experiencing trials, he becomes courageous and empathetic.

32
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:36,500
He learned to listen to the emotions in poetry and learned to face himself.

33
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:43,000
From this growth of not understanding to understanding, just like many people's process of learning poetry, I think it's quite interesting.

34
00:03:43,500 --> 00:03:54,000
I also like it because he felt intimidated by the poets, but he had to overcome difficulties in the poetic realm, and finally found his courage.

35
00:03:55,000 --> 00:04:03,500
Exactly. I think from being very intimidated at the beginning, to finally overcoming difficulties and finding courage. This process is very worth us learning from.

36
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:14,000
So, if you were Liu Zhongyuan today, which poetic realm in the book would you most want to challenge, and why?

37
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:22,500
I would want to challenge Jiang Xue, because of the scenery of mountains and rivers, the unique landscape of Gu Zhou. I really want to experience it.

38
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:32,000
If I could search for poetic souls in the snow, it would mean learning how to coexist with loneliness. Such a trial, though cold, is very pure.

39
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:42,000
I want to challenge the poetic realm of mountains and rivers, expressing my emotions and thoughts through the scenery of nature.

40
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:52,500
Wow, just now hearing classmate En Fu talk like that, I feel like the teacher can really feel the scenery of Gu Zhou and Qian Shan, and really wants to experience it together.

41
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:59,500
The book also constantly mentions poetic souls. Do you think finding poetic souls is difficult or not? How would you do it?

42
00:05:00,500 --> 00:05:09,000
It should be a bit difficult, because each poetic soul is in the poet's situation. Not only do you have to break through, but you also have to truly understand the meaning of that poem.

43
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:20,000
I would try to calm my mind and observe the details in life, finding poetic souls from nature, life, or emotions that move people.

44
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:27,500
Exactly. Finding poetic souls, I also feel it's very difficult. It requires us to deeply feel the poet's thoughts.

45
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:34,000
So, does this book change your impression of Tang poetry?

46
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:44,500
Yes. I now feel that each poem is like a small world. It carries the poet's feelings and stories. And now when I recite poetry, I will start to think about what the poet was thinking, what they saw, their feelings.

47
00:05:51,000 --> 00:06:01,500
It changed Tang poetry from being difficult to memorize to believing that Tang poetry is full of wonder and vitality.

48
00:06:02,500 --> 00:06:09,000
Great! I also look forward to you using this poetic realm in other readings, and you can share with the teacher often.

49
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:12,000
So, I'd like to ask, what do you think is the meaning of poetic soul?

50
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:28,000
In Chinese culture, "poetic soul" actually has many meanings. Today I want to share about history and culture. For example, Qu Yuan. I can call him a "loyal soul," because he wrote a small poem about protecting the country's ideals with his life. And Li Bai is definitely a "free soul." His works are unrestrained and free.

51
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:42,500
Du Fu is a "melancholy soul." The melancholy here refers to the melancholy of the state. He wrote about the suffering of the times with sincere laments.

52
00:06:43,500 --> 00:06:50,500
I think it's like the soul of poetry, containing the poet's joy, anger, love, and happiness.

53
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:56,500
Exactly. You can only grasp the poetic soul by feeling the poet's character and situation.

54
00:06:57,000 --> 00:07:02,000
So, how would you want to search for poetic souls or inspiration?

55
00:07:04,000 --> 00:07:19,000
Normally, if I want to find poetic souls, I would put on headphones and listen to music I like. Inspiration is like poetic souls. It's not that the tighter you grasp, the more you find. It's that when you calm your mind, it will come to you.

56
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:28,000
I would keep a diary or listen to music, transforming feelings into words, rediscovering creativity and passion.

57
00:07:29,000 --> 00:07:37,000
Excellent! Classmates, after reading "Soul of Poetry," which part would you most want to recommend to your good friends, and why?

58
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:47,000
I would want to recommend Liu Zhongyuan's first entry into the poetic realm and his discovery of the poetic soul. This part is both magical and interesting, full of a sense of adventure.

59
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:50,000
Through his perspective, there's a sense of spiritual transcendence.

60
00:07:51,000 --> 00:08:05,000
I would recommend the part about Liu Zhongyuan searching for poetic souls, because it makes me feel that the poet, despite experiencing hardships, can still find their belief and hope in words.

61
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:11,000
Does this book give you any new ideas about writing or creation, or about poetry?

62
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:23,000
I've begun to understand that creation can be like an adventure. Every word has life, can be arranged, can lead the reader into it. It's a very strong sense of expression.

63
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:31,000
I found that writing poetry doesn't necessarily require flowery words, but rather expressing inner feelings truthfully.

64
00:08:32,500 --> 00:09:07,000
Exactly. Today, we and two classmates from 802 have entered the world of poetic souls. In fact, reading is not just about memorizing words. More importantly, use your heart to feel, to imagine, to experience every scene. Just as the classmates mentioned earlier, when we bravely face challenges, pour in our feelings, and even feel that noble, serene, and detached atmosphere, the poetic soul will appear. I also hope everyone can find their own poetic soul in reading, turn words into scenes, turn them into feelings, and start their own fantasy journey. Thank you to the two classmates for their wonderful sharing. Today's Jianhua Love Poetry ends here. I'm Teacher Zi Qiao.

65
00:09:15,000 --> 00:09:16,500
